  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Code Files**\n\nI\'m currently focused on three files: `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, and `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`. I\'m starting with `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, meticulously verifying its import of `createDirect`. I\'ll proceed cautiously, ensuring a thorough understanding of this file before tackling the others.\n\n\n**Implementing Mouse Steering**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated `DirectMouseEvaluation` and related types from `./MouseResponseCurve`, re-exporting the mouse steering functions without causing any disruptions. Now, I\'m adding zero-allocation scratch fields to `FlightController`, including `directMouseEval` and `directCurveParams`, and initializing the `steeringMode`. The next step is updating the `FlightController.update(...)` method.\n\n\n**Refining Flight Steering**\n\nI\'ve just finished clamping independent yaw and pitch rates to `STEERING_BOUNDS` and scaling them by hull class ratios, achieving zero allocations by populating `this.directCurveParams` in-place. The next action is calling `evaluateDirectMouseSteering` with the mouse deltas and safe delta-time, followed by blending in optional arrow-key steering, ensuring values are properly clamped.\n\n\n**Smoothing Input Signals**\n\nI\'m now incorporating minimal input smoothing using `stepDirectAngularRate` for both yaw and pitch, along with the safe delta time and input smoothing settings. I\'ve also begun work on updating the visual aim reticle within the independent rounded-rectangle aim boundary. I\'m calculating the desired offset based on live turn demand, and this will be scaled using the hull class ratios from my earlier computations.\n\n\n**Finalizing Flight Control**\n\nI\'m now integrating the aim cursor logic, ensuring it remains within the rounded-rectangle boundary. I\'m updating `aimCursorX` and `aimCursorY` with normalized coordinates from the clamp. The telemetry fields are being updated with `joystickEval`, ensuring visual feedback aligns consistently. Then, I will address the preserved baseline logic, and finally ensure the other steps, like roll, quaternion rotation, and telemetry, remain clean.\n\n\n"
