    modified_response: "### STARFALL \342\200\224 Precision + Fast Turning Calibration Summary\n\n#### 1. Implemented Features\n- **Direct Arcade Nonlinear Mouse Response Curve (`src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`)**:\n  - Converts Pointer Lock relative deltas (`movementX`, `movementY`) over frame delta `dt` (clamped at `velDt = max(dt, 1/240)` for frame-rate independence) into instantaneous mouse speed `v = hypot(vx, vy)` in CSS `px/s`.\n  - **Documented Input Normalization Range**: `inputNormalizationRange = 1600 px/s` (`26.67 px/frame` at 60 FPS), yielding normalized input `u = (v * mouseSensitivity) / 1600`.\n  - **Continuous Nonlinear Gain Curve**:\n    $$g(u) = a \\cdot u + (1 - a) \\cdot u^{p}$$\n    with `a = precisionLinearBlend = 0.25` (keeps 1\342\200\2232 px micro-corrections subtle and predictable with zero deadzone cliff) and `p = responseCurve = 1.85` (smoothly amplifies medium and large mouse sweeps; reduces cleanly to linear `g(u) = u` when `p = 1.0`).\n  - **C2-Continuous Soft Saturation**: `softSaturateSigned` is exact identity for `|x| <= 0.85` and transitions via `0.85 + 0.15 * tanh((|x| - 0.85) / 0.15)` above `0.85`, preventing clipping corners or sensitivity spikes when approaching max turn rate.\n  - **Zero-Drift Stopping**: Optional minimal smoothing (`inputSmoothing`, default `0.08` \342\206\222 `4ms` time constant) applies a `2.5x` stop-decay multiplier and snaps rates `< 0.005 rad/s` to `0` when mouse input stops, eliminating lingering rotation and drift.\n- **Independent Aim Boundary & Baseline Preservation**:\n  - `AimBoundary.ts` and `InputManager.ts` remain untouched. The rounded-rectangle aim boundary (`30% W \303\227 35% H`) is strictly decoupled from the response curve; in direct mode, the HUD aim reticle reflects live turn demand inside the boundary and self-centers when input stops.\n  - The pre-calibration configuration and execution path are preserved verbatim in `BASELINE_STEERING_CONFIG` and `FlightController.steeringMode = \'virtual-joystick-baseline\'` so this calibration can be reverted independently via `STEERING_CONFIG.steeringMode`.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Exact Parameters Changed / Added\n\n| Parameter | Previous Baseline | Calibrated Default | Configurable Range | Purpose |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| `steeringMode` | Virtual joystick | `\'direct-nonlinear\'` | `\'direct-nonlinear\' \\| \'virtual-joystick-baseline\'` | Active steering model (toggle to revert independently) |\n| `inputNormalizationRange` | \342\200\224 | `1600 px/s` | Fixed reference | Reference mouse speed (`u = 1.0` at `1.0x` sensitivity; `26.67 px/f` @ 60 FPS) |\n| `mouseSensitivity` | `1.0` | `1.0` | `0.30` \342\200\223 `2.50` | Base mouse sensitivity (independent of curve & ceilings) |\n| `responseCurve` | `1.35` (radial) | `1.85` (velocity) | `1.00` \342\200\223 `2.60` | Nonlinear response curve exponent (`1.0` = linear) |\n| `precisionLinearBlend` | `0.85` (inner radial) | `0.25` | Config constant | Low-speed linear precision floor `a` |\n| `softSaturationKnee` | Hard clamp at `1.0` | `0.85` | Config constant | C2-continuous soft ceiling transition point |\n| `maxYawRate` | `profile.yawSpeed * 2.0` (`4.2`) | `3.5 rad/s` (~200.5\302\260/s) | `1.5` \342\200\223 `5.5 rad/s` | Independent max yaw rate (ref Interceptor; scales per hull class) |\n| `maxPitchRate` | `profile.pitchSpeed * 2.0` (`3.9`) | `3.0 rad/s` (~171.9\302\260/s) | `1.5` \342\200\223 `5.0 rad/s` | Independent max pitch rate (ref Interceptor; scales per hull class) |\n| `yawSensitivity` | `1.0` | `1.0` | `0.40` \342\200\223 `1.80` | Independent horizontal yaw sensitivity balance |\n| `pitchSensitivity` | `0.9` | `0.9` | `0.40` \342\200\223 `1.80` | Independent vertical pitch sensitivity balance |\n| `inputSmoothing` | `angularAccel: 18`, `damping: 14` | `0.08` (`4 ms` tau) | `0.00` (Off) \342\200\223 `0.40` | Optional minimal micro-jitter smoothing with immediate stop |\n| `joystickRadius` (Aim Boundary) | `1.0` (`30%\303\22735%`) | `1.0` (`30%\303\22735%`) | `0.65` \342\200\223 `1.50` | Visual aim boundary scale (strictly independent of curve) |\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Files & Systems Changed\n- `src/config/steering.ts`: Added `DIRECT_MOUSE_STEERING_CONFIG`, preserved `BASELINE_STEERING_CONFIG`, updated `STEERING_CONFIG` and `STEERING_BOUNDS`.\n- `src/engine/MouseResponseCurve.ts`: Added pure, zero-allocation nonlinear mouse response curve, C2 soft-saturation, and minimal smoothing module.\n- `src/engine/FlightController.ts`: Integrated `direct-nonlinear` steering pipeline while preserving the `virtual-joystick-baseline` branch and keeping `AimBoundary` independent.\n- `src/types/game.ts`: Added `maxYawRate`, `maxPitchRate`, and `inputSmoothing` to `GameSettings`.\n- `src/config/ships.ts`: Updated `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` and added clean `starfall.settings.v7` migration from `v6`.\n- `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`: Updated `SteeringCurvePreview` to plot the nonlinear mouse response curve vs linear reference, and exposed separate sliders for Base Sensitivity, Response Curve, Max Yaw Rate, Max Pitch Rate, Yaw Balance, Pitch Balance, Input Smoothing, and Aim Boundary.\n- `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`: Hid the virtual-joystick deadzone box when `steeringMode === \'direct-nonlinear\'` while preserving the rounded-rectangle aim boundary, reticles, and tether.\n- **Unchanged systems**: `InputManager.ts`, `AimBoundary.ts`, `CameraController.ts`, `CombatManager.ts`, `GameScene.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Tests Performed & Verified Results\n- **Typecheck & Build**: `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`) and Vite production build (`compile_applet`) passed with zero errors; dev server verified responding `HTTP 200` on port `3000`.\n- **Automated Engine Simulation Suite (`tsx` directly against `FlightController` & `MouseResponseCurve`)**:\n  - **Curve Continuity & Monotonicity** (`500` samples across `u \342\210\210 [0, 2.0]`): Strictly monotonic, max step jump `0.006107`, smooth saturation to `1.000000`, zero abrupt spikes.\n  - **Speed Spectrum (60 FPS, default settings)**:\n    - Very small (`0.5 px/f` = `30 px/s`): `0.018 rad/s` (`1.0\302\260/s`, `3.45\302\260/100px`)\n    - Very small (`1 px/f` = `60 px/s`): `0.039 rad/s` (`2.2\302\260/s`, `3.71\302\260/100px`)\n    - Precision (`2 px/f` = `120 px/s`): `0.087 rad/s` (`5.0\302\260/s`, `4.17\302\260/100px`)\n    - Slow tracking (`5 px/f` = `300 px/s`): `0.283 rad/s` (`16.2\302\260/s`, `5.40\302\260/100px`)\n    - Medium tracking (`10 px/f` = `600 px/s`): `0.756 rad/s` (`43.3\302\260/s`, `7.22\302\260/100px`)\n    - Medium-fast (`16 px/f` = `960 px/s`): `1.545 rad/s` (`88.5\302\260/s`, `9.22\302\260/100px`)\n    - Fast turn (`25 px/f` = `1500 px/s`): `3.144 rad/s` (`180.1\302\260/s`, `12.01\302\260/100px` \342\200\224 **3.24\303\227** stronger per-pixel response than 1 px micro-aiming)\n    - Large rapid sweep (`35\342\200\22350 px/f` = `2100\342\200\2233000 px/s`): smoothly capped at `3.500 rad/s` (`200.5\302\260/s`)\n  - **Frame-Rate Independence**: Over `0.5 s` at `300 px/s` \342\206\222 `8.10\302\260` (30 FPS) / `8.09\302\260` (60 FPS) / `8.08\302\260` (120 FPS); at `1200 px/s` \342\206\222 `62.96\302\260` (30 FPS) / `62.93\302\260` (60 FPS) / `62.82\302\260` (120 FPS).\n  - **Rapid Direction Reversal (`+25 px/f \342\206\222 -25 px/f`)**: Reversed sign on frame 1 (`-3.1437 rad/s \342\206\222 +3.1334 rad/s`).\n  - **Immediate Stop After Full Turn (`-3.500 rad/s` yaw, `-2.986 rad/s` pitch)**: Frame 1 velocity dropped to `yaw = 0`, `pitch = 0`; total drift over 20 subsequent zero-input frames = `0.000000\302\260`; reticle self-centered to `{ x: 0, y: 0 }`.\n  - **Parameter Isolation & Aim Boundary Decoupling**: Confirmed resizing `joystickRadius` (`1.0 \342\206\222 1.45`) leaves yaw/pitch rates unchanged (`< 1e-12`), and `maxYawRate`, `maxPitchRate`, `yawSensitivity`, `pitchSensitivity` each modify only their own axis.\n  - **Baseline Rollback Check**: Confirmed `flight.steeringMode = \'virtual-joystick-baseline\'` executes cleanly.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Remaining Issues & Recommended Next Step\n- **Live Browser Interactive Testing**: No headless Chromium/Playwright binary is installed in this environment, so real-mouse physical Pointer Lock feel (fine aiming at moving bots, continuous edge turning, and physical DPI feel) has not yet been exercised in an interactive browser session.\n- **Recommended Next Step**: Playtest Mission 01 in your browser with Pointer Lock engaged across micro-aiming, slow lead-pip tracking, 180\302\260 turns, and sudden stops; if you want a slightly gentler or faster transition, fine-tune `responseCurve` (`1.60`\342\200\223`2.10`), `maxYawRate`/`maxPitchRate`, or `mouseSensitivity` live in the Settings panel and share the feel feedback for a final constant lock-in."
